&lt;li&gt;Manage the employee lifecycle for Fulfillment Center, Logistics, and Regional employees from onboarding through offboarding, including orientation, performance management, corrective action, and terminations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the on-site People Partner Generalist for TX sites with regional support across both locations providing daily HR support across benefits, payroll, attendance, policies, compliance, and employee relations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support implementation of corporate-wide policies, procedures, systems, and initiatives, including change management efforts such as WMS implementation and operational growth initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching, direction, and counsel to frontline managers and supervisors to proactively anticipate, prevent, and resolve a wide range of HR issues; independently lead investigations and employee relations cases and escalate as needed to the Senior Manager, Employee Relations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage workers’ compensation cases from incident through resolution in partnership with vendors, insurers, and the Insurance &amp;amp; Risk Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with site leadership to drive employee engagement and retention initiatives for frontline teams and reinforce leadership expectations around fair and consistent people management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify trends in employee relations, attendance, safety, and turnover; proactively assess risk and recommend practical, business-aligned solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver, coordinate, and track required training to ensure compliance with local, state, OSHA, and company requirements; provide individual and group training on HR policies, procedures, performance management, and leadership capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support program management efforts including Supervisor Trainee Program coordination, development plan tracking, compliance initiatives, and process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Answer and assist site leadership and regional teams with general HR questions and requests while ensuring compliance and consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with HR reporting, documentation, case tracking, and compliance records to maintain accurate and organized HR operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree required or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of HR Generalist or People Partner experience in field-based, multi-site, fulfillment, logistics, or operational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing day-to-day HR administration including employee relations, workers’ compensation, compliance, onboarding, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of employment law and OSHA requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to support hourly and frontline workforces in fast-paced operational settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, prioritization, and problem-solving skills with the ability to balance empathy and firm, fair decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with strong attention to detail, especially in case documentation and compliance tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starting, resourceful, and action-oriented with the ability to operate independently while knowing when to escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in high-growth, fast-moving, and sometimes ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel across TX locations;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekend work may be required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HR certification (SHRM-CP or PHR) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual (English and Spanish or Mandarin) preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
